  "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-8 \\\\  & y+2z=-1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(2)=-1\\,\u27f9\\,y=-1-4=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(-5)+(2)=-8\\,\u27f9\\,x=-8+10-2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-5$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e80,-5,2\u27e9.$",
